From 93aa5c5d74ab4f906f35d025c5a1ceb9e8c756f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 01:41:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/evdi: add the Rust virtual display driver

Add a Rust implementation of EVDI while preserving the established libevdi
and DisplayLinkManager display ABI. Install that ABI as a normal DRM UAPI
header, use generated Rust UAPI bindings, and translate its pointer-bearing
ioctls for 32-bit clients.

Create cards through the established platform sysfs interface and expose
the expected DRM ioctls and events. Use owned DRM, KMS, event, framebuffer,
and sysfs abstractions throughout; the driver contains no `unsafe` block,
no direct `bindings::` call and no reconstructed object lifetime.

Prepare a bounded four-entry scanout pool with owned shmem mappings so
compositor swapchain buffers are mapped before notifying the client and
reused for later flips and GRABPIX calls. Enforce the bandwidth limits
supplied by userspace without applying a driver-invented multiplier.

Advertise a cursor plane, so the compositor keeps the pointer out of the
primary framebuffer instead of dirtying the desktop on every movement.
Reporting it to the client is opt-in through EVDI_ENABLE_CURSOR_EVENTS: a
client that has not asked composites the pointer itself and must not also
receive it out of band. The bitmap accompanies a shape change as a GEM
handle minted in the client's own file, which is why it goes through the
event channel's connected-file borrow rather than being sent under the
event lock.

Apply the CRTC's CTM and GAMMA_LUT in software on the way to the client.
EVDI has no colour hardware, so a compositor correcting through those
properties -- which is what GNOME's Night Light and KDE's Night Colour do
-- otherwise has nowhere to put the correction. color.rs is shared verbatim
with drm/vino, which has the same problem and no way to share a crate with
a separate module.

Replay the current mode from CONNECT. MODE_CHANGED is an edge, so a client
attaching to a card the compositor already configured would otherwise wait
forever for an announcement that has already happened, with its display
dark.

DDC/CI remains an ABI-compatible no-op: the driver does not register a
virtual I2C adapter until a Rust I2C provider API can express the adapter
lifetime safely.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
